<item><title>Mbabane council plans E191.4 million growth budget</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/mbabane-council-plans-e191-4-million-growth-budget-d0fcbf/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/mbabane-council-plans-e191-4-million-growth-budget-d0fcbf/</guid><category>Eswatini</category><description>The Mbabane Municipal Council has drafted a 2027/28 budget focused on service delivery and infrastructure, with property taxes forming 91 percent of projected income.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:27:57 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/mbabane-council-plans-e191-4-million-growth-budget-d0fcbf/share.jpg" length="40345" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/mbabane-council-plans-e191-4-million-growth-budget-d0fcbf/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
